module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.arrow_domain_meaning_is_not_carried_on_the_node

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data arrow_domain_meaning_is_not_carried_on_the_node: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "arrow_domain_meaning_is_not_carried_on_the_node" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**an Arrow's first positional child means different things in different producers -- a parameter list of Named binders, one positional argument TYPE, or one record-typed payload -- and the Node does not say which, so every reader guesses from SHAPE, and a producer or fixture that builds the other meaning gets a reader's answer for the wrong one** (THE INVALID STATE is a well-formed Node whose domain a reader interprets under a meaning its producer did not intend. Readers read `first(children)` or the first positional child and treat a Named Conj there as a parameter list: `v2.std.node` `arrow_domain_binder_labels`, the resolve and symbol-index Arrow arms, infer's formal readers, and `v2.compiler.target_serialize` `type_expr_arrow_split_from_types`, which reads 'every positional but the last' as inputs.)",

    "THE HARM is a wrong answer or a binding-time refusal at a reader far from the producer that caused it, and it is reached only when some claim happens to exercise that reader. Four receipts: (1) gunbc#12361 gave an Arrow a required signature-order edge; hand-built fixtures that did not know it were refused at binding time (`application_parameter_order_absent`) and ten claims went false, all outside the required floor's executed population (that population half is the landed row [[green_floor_executes_no_claim_whose_verdict_a_body_change_can_move]], not this one). (2) Service operations lowered their input payload as a Named Conj in domain position, so resolve bound the payload's field names as scope locals and `symbol_index_fill` indexed them at the operation. (3) `symbol_index_fill` consulted `v2.extdeps.languages.dag` `namespace_graft_spine_segment_edge_optional`, which reads ANY Conj with one Named edge to a Conj as a dotted-name spine segment, so a one-record-parameter domain lost its parameter level (repaired for Arrow domains in gunbc#12501; the shape-based recognizer was then deleted in gunbc#12611, and `namespace_graft_spine_body_optional` recognizes a segment only when its chain ends at the graft's body mark). (4) Resolve and symbol_index_fill read `first(children)` rather than the first positional child, so a Named edge placed first would be read as the domain (gunbc#12499, subsumed by #12501, with a discriminating red executed on main).",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. Two Arrow ENCODINGS coexisted, a DESIGN section 3 fork in its own right: E1, the declared signature (`v2.std.arrow_signature` `declared_signature`: a Named-binder domain plus the signature-order edge), and E2, a positional-type Arrow `[T1 .. Tn, U]` (the algebra's operation signatures, the emitted add-fn Arrow in 14 language models, fn-type lowering, and the v1 host seam `v2.std.decl_index` `export_signature_facts`). Program P (gunbc#12625) retired E2: every former producer now builds through `declared_signature` or `v2.std.arrow_signature` `anonymous_signature_arrow` (e.g. `v2.std.algebra_structure_signature` `algebra_binary_fn_node`, moved out of `v2.std.algebra` to sit above `arrow_signature`), and `v2.compiler.translate` `translate_arrow_signature_split` reads inputs only through `arrow_declared_parameter_order`. A third meaning, the operation payload, is resolved by making the payload ONE positional argument of record type (Y-wrap, gunbc#12501). The order edge is NOT derivable from the domain: `v2.std.node` `kind_edge_discipline` never reads the parent and content hashing sorts a Named Conj, so deleting the edge would make `f(a,b)` and `f(b,a)` one identity. A construction seal through `declared_signature` was considered and REFUSED: the Arrow kind reaches Node through generic builders a literal seal never sees, and sealing the value refuses every recognizer.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: 1. Each meaning conflict surfaced as a wrong answer or a binding-time refusal inside some claim, and only when a claim reached the reader. CEILING 3, structurally guaranteed: once one encoding holds, whether a Named-binder domain lacks its order edge is decidable from the Node alone (a domain with no Named binder is sound without one, since its order is positional and hashing keeps it), so well-formedness can refuse the bad state wherever a Node is admitted.",

    "CLIMBED TO CEILING 3 BY A4 (the next-rung trigger, A SINGLE ARROW ENCODING, was held by Program P, gunbc#12625). `v2.std.node` `arrow_signature_order_conforms` now answers an absent order edge with `!arrow_domain_binds_a_name`: an Arrow whose domain -- its first positional child -- is a Conj carrying any Named binder, with no ^arrow_signature_order_edge, is ill formed at Node admission, reversing #12361's 'an order-less Arrow is well formed'. A domain that binds no name owes no order and stays admitted. THE RUNG IS THE MINIMUM ACROSS ADMISSION PATHS, each executed by a discriminating RED plus positive controls in `v2.test.claim.arrow_order_edge.admission_wall`: `v2.compiler.infer` `infer` (which now gates its entry on well_formed, since it is entered directly with a ResolvedTree), `v2.compiler.resolve` `resolve`, and the `assemble_program_from_ingest` root gate `v2.compiler.name_resolve` `validate_module_roots`. The binding-time refusal stays enrolled as its own path (`v2.test.claim.declared_parameter_order` `dpo_binding_refuses_an_arrow_without_order`), and `dpo_positional_binding_refuses_an_arrow_without_order` is flipped to assert ill-formedness and stays enrolled.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.arrow_signature", decl_name: "declared_signature", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.node", decl_name: "arrow_signature_order_conforms", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.node", decl_name: "arrow_domain_binds_a_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.arrow_order_edge.admission_wall", decl_name: "aoe_infer_refuses_a_named_domain_without_order", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.arrow_order_edge.admission_wall", decl_name: "aoe_resolve_refuses_a_named_domain_without_order", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.test.claim.arrow_order_edge.admission_wall", decl_name: "aoe_assembly_gate_refuses_a_named_domain_without_order", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.node", decl_name: "arrow_domain_binder_labels", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.algebra_structure_signature", decl_name: "algebra_binary_fn_node", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.arrow_signature", decl_name: "anonymous_signature_arrow", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.target_serialize", decl_name: "type_expr_arrow_split_from_types", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.extdeps.languages.dag", decl_name: "namespace_graft_spine_body_optional", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
